    "ctest": [
      "aero.global_geometry",
      "coupling.case_uniform_flow",
      "structure.pg_prepared_patch",
      "structure.pg_full_trace"
    ],
    "catch": "2492 assertions on the end-to-end fixture with seed 23 in each configuration.",
    "oracle": "For a flat 2 m thick reference with an independent constant-curvature deformation, at s=3/4 the upper surface has z=41/32, Vz=9/16 and normal slope -3/4. An explicit interior chart zeta=(s-3/4)/4 predicts z=9/32 and slopes (1,0,1) and (0,1,0) at the collocation. Compare the actual native nonpenetration to (127/12500-9/16)/sqrt(2), with ambient converted independently from 2 ft/min. The exact planar control predicts 127/12500-9/16.",
    "negative": "Reject changed patch, changed geometry generation, swapped reference vertex material points, zero work, and reuse of actual load results from a different trial stamp or same-stamp changed geometry. Keep the registered vertex alias on its canonical point and each load on one vertex.",
    "static": "Windows and Linux clang-tidy 21.1.1 on five product/test translation units, pinned clang-format 21.1.2, trace-check, recorded SHA256 and Japanese prose lint.",
    "mutation": "Omitting the zeta Jacobian column in an isolated GCC build caused both the curved interior slope assertion and the original residual assertion to fail (Catch2 exit 42). Byte-identical restoration passed all 2492 assertions."
  },
